      padWork: { description: "Holding positions: Partner holds pads for charge/defense practice, provides resistance for hand fighting, absorbs impact for push mechanics. Strike sequences: called combinations (charge-thrust-push), progressive resistance (light → firm → reactive). Cues: Partner provides verbal/visual triggers, moves with wrestler to simulate opponent reactions, gives feedback on technique efficiency." },
      sparring: { description: "Live Sumo: Light to hard intensity based on mutual agreement and experience levels. Focus: applying techniques live against resisting opponent, developing timing and pressure management. Structure: 3-5 min rounds / 1 min rest between rounds. Safety: controlled intensity, no slamming or dangerous moves, respect training partners' experience levels, stop immediately on injury or discomfort, debrief briefly after rounds for learning." },
      formKata: { description: "Sumo does not use traditional forms/kata. Replaced by 'Kimarite Drilling': repeating specific winning techniques (e.g., oshi-dashi, uwatenage) to build muscle memory and timing. Purpose: technique refinement, pressure testing, developing instinctive responses. Progression: slow motion with perfect form → add speed → add light resistance → full resistance → live application in sumo." }
